# L §5.9 Rows replaced: "a patch there is refused (LOAD-REPLACE) under every cut that sees the version" (L §8.3
# `replace rows of <b> in <V> patch no table on <span>`). v2's replace rows [0, 10] and (20, inf) match v1's intervals
# and leave a gap, so they are a patch, not a whole table; v2 governs 2027.. and v1 only 2026..2027, so from 2028 the
# patch meets no table: refused at load, though no ask reads 2028 (snap11 refused it only at such a read; writer 8,
# sixth pass, beside C3-16). L5_9_patch_covered: the same patch governing 2027 loads.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2028-12-31

source s "s"
band b(n: int): int
input mid: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..2027
  known 2025-12-01
  b: [0, 10] = 1
  b: (10, 20] = 2
  b: (20, inf) = 3

version facts
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  mid = 15

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  replace b: [0, 10] = 5
  replace b: (20, inf) = 6

ask q1: b(mid) law 2027-06-30
ask q3: b(mid) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-REPLACE replace rows of b in v2 patch no table on 2028-01-01.. ...
